          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: the review is blocked by missing cost-event records\n\nI verified the relevant work order and September Pending Close time, but **cannot determine whether a late event occurred** because the supporting cost-event input was not staged and returned “Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation/product | Modine Racine — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 / PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Source transaction ID | Unavailable |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event record |\n\nThe timestamp is reproduced exactly as recorded; the source supplies no timezone. The readable records contain work orders and cost periods, but no cost-event rows. **That absence is not evidence that no late event exists.**\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B documentation states that new transactions created after Pending Close, relating to the current or a prior period, are **not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, including those in error. Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions that continue processing.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary manufacturing cost transaction newly created after **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** should be held rather than processed while September remains Pending Close. The missing event’s type, creation time, and recorded status are necessary for an event-specific consistency conclusion.\n\n*Policy source: “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” Oracle 26B PDF page 233, printed page 225.*\n\nNo database records were changed. I submitted the partial report, which remains marked **needs evidence**, and saved the audit result and provenance at `/cache/work/worker_f1214f4d6944/audit-report.json`.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
